# Docker workflow (PyTorchSim)

## Default image

- Use the pinned image in `docker_run.sh`: `ghcr.io/psal-postech/torchsim-ci:v1.0.1`.

## Preferred run pattern

Use a unique container name, set the working directory, keep IPC host, and remove on exit:

```bash
timestamp=$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S)
docker run -it --ipc=host --rm \
  --name "torchsim_${USER}_${timestamp}" \
  -w /workspace/PyTorchSim \
  ghcr.io/psal-postech/torchsim-ci:v1.0.1 \
  bash
```

## When you need to persist changes

By default, the container has no access to your local repo. If you want edits/results to persist, mount the repo into the container:

```bash
timestamp=$(date +%Y%m%d%H%M%S)
docker run -it --ipc=host --rm \
  --name "torchsim_${USER}_${timestamp}" \
  -v "$PWD:/workspace/PyTorchSim" \
  -w /workspace/PyTorchSim \
  ghcr.io/psal-postech/torchsim-ci:v1.0.1 \
  bash
```

## GPU usage (only if the host supports it)

If NVIDIA Container Toolkit is installed and GPUs should be exposed:

```bash
docker run -it --rm --ipc=host --gpus all \
  -v "$PWD:/workspace/PyTorchSim" -w /workspace/PyTorchSim \
  ghcr.io/psal-postech/torchsim-ci:v1.0.1 bash
```

If `--gpus all` fails, prefer fixing host tooling rather than changing project code.

## Outputs and git hygiene

- Write run artifacts under `output/`, `outputs/`, or `togsim_results/` (already ignored by `.gitignore`).
- Do not commit generated artifacts (logs, results folders, notebooks checkpoints).

## Troubleshooting quick checks

- **Can't see repo files in container**: you likely forgot `-v "$PWD:/workspace/PyTorchSim"`.
- **Permission issues writing outputs**: check host directory permissions; consider `-u "$(id -u):$(id -g)"` if the image supports it.
- **Shared memory / dataloader hangs**: keep `--ipc=host` (as in `docker_run.sh`).

